  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "MoEngage has given you two trees T1T_1T1​ and T2T_2T2​. Both trees have NNN nodes and are rooted at node 111.\n\nDefinitions:\n\n\nLCA1(u,v)=LCA_1(u,v) = LCA1​(u,v)= Lowest common ancestor of node uuu and node vvv in tree T1T_1T1​.\nLCA2(u,v)=LCA_2(u,v) = LCA2​(u,v)= Lowest common ancestor of node uuu and node vvv in tree T2T_2T2​.\nH1(v)=H_1(v) = H1​(v)= Number of nodes in the shortest path from node 111 to node vvv in tree T1T_1T1​. Note that, H1(1)=1H_1(1) = 1H1​(1)=1.\nH2(v)=H_2(v) = H2​(v)= Number of nodes in the shortest path from node 111 to node vvv in tree T2T_2T2​. Note that, H2(1)=1H_2(1) = 1H2​(1)=1.\nFind the **maximum** value of H1(LCA1(u,v))+H2(LCA2(u,v))H_1(LCA_1(u,v)) + H_2(LCA_2(u,v))H1​(LCA1​(u,v))+H2​(LCA2​(u,v)) over all pairs (u,v)(u,v)(u,v) such that u≠vu \\neq vu=v.\n\nMore formally, find max⁡1≤u&lt;v≤N[H1(LCA1(u,v))+H2(LCA2(u,v))]\\max\\limits_{1 \\leq u \\lt v \\leq N} [H_1(LCA_1(u,v)) + H_2(LCA_2(u,v))]1≤u&lt;v≤Nmax​[H1​(LCA1​(u,v))+H2​(LCA2​(u,v))].\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nFirst line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, the number of nodes.\nEach of the next (N−1)(N - 1)(N−1) lines contain two integers uuu and vvv denoting an edge between nodes uuu and vvv in tree T1T_1T1​.\nEach of the next (N−1)(N - 1)(N−1) lines contain two integers uuu and vvv denoting an edge between nodes uuu and vvv in tree T2T_2T2​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output in a single line max⁡1≤u&lt;v≤N[H1(LCA1(u,v))+H2(LCA2(u,v))]\\max\\limits_{1 \\leq u \\lt v \\leq N} [H_1(LCA_1(u,v)) + H_2(LCA_2(u,v))]1≤u&lt;v≤Nmax​[H1​(LCA1​(u,v))+H2​(LCA2​(u,v))].",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\leq N \\leq 10^52≤N≤105",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
